   $q$The author writes that changing the order of the day "costs almost nothing." How does this wording help the author's purpose?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It explains exactly how much the cafeteria workers would be paid for planning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows that the school board has plenty of extra money to spend on lunch.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It admits that the plan is too expensive to try during the next school year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-purpose"},{"text":"It makes the change seem small and easy, so readers feel safer supporting it.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It makes the change seem small and easy, so readers feel safer supporting it.$q$, $q$By stressing how little the change costs, the author makes the request sound low risk, which helps persuade readers. The phrase is about the plan being cheap, not about the board having spare money.$q$, 'draft', '85785a5a-45db-5ed3-ba2b-1481042cc4ef')
