   $q$What is the purpose of the example about the four drawings of a cat?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To show how keeping mistakes lets an artist see their own improvement.","is_correct":true},{"text":"To suggest that artists should draw the same subject four times every day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"To prove that cats are the hardest animal for young artists to draw well.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"To explain why the author tears out pages that contain clumsy drawings.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-position"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To show how keeping mistakes lets an artist see their own improvement.$q$, $q$The example comes right after "you erase the record of your own learning" and says the pages show "exactly how you improved." The cat is just a sample subject, not a claim about cats being hard to draw.$q$, 'draft', '86ddb0ce-77a6-5278-ae87-3764d4d439a1')
