   $q$In the first paragraph, the author writes, "I understand the feeling." Why does the author include this sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To admit that the author also tears out pages and plans to keep doing so.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To agree that students are right to erase every mistake from their pages.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-position"},{"text":"To change the topic from sketchbooks to the feelings of professional artists.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"To show sympathy, so readers who hide their work feel more open to the advice.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To show sympathy, so readers who hide their work feel more open to the advice.$q$, $q$The sentence is followed by "but I want to make a case for the messy sketchbook," so it builds trust before disagreeing. The author does not agree that erasing every mistake is right.$q$, 'draft', '86ddb0ce-77a6-5278-ae87-3764d4d439a1')
