   $q$How does the author keep the passage balanced?$q$, $q$[{"text":"By refusing to share any facts so that readers can make up their own minds.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"By letting a student and a teacher argue with each other about the two choices.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"By giving one paragraph to the strengths of screens and one to those of paper.","is_correct":true},{"text":"By listing only the problems with screens and only the problems with paper.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By giving one paragraph to the strengths of screens and one to those of paper.$q$, $q$Paragraph 2 begins "Screens offer convenience," and paragraph 3 begins "Printed books have advantages of their own," giving each side fair space. The passage focuses on strengths, not only problems, and it does include facts.$q$, 'draft', 'b88db7c0-80f6-59a6-b769-ab4b78cfad92')
